Z||000005||CoryFiero||12-16-2001||11:14 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.cybercars.com/mnfr/fierohq/dgauges.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cybercars.com/mnfr/fierohq/dgauges.html</A> <P>check this out, they are pretty expensive but they are pretty kool, Im thinking about buying a set,<P>Also I have a q here, if I get the "other" gauges that were found in the later style fieros I think only the v-6's? Well If I got the digital ones of them could I hook them up to my 4 cyl, until I upgrade to somthing bigger (V8 hehehehe), I have the surround in my new dash (pisas wrap around) but the holes will be empty without them, will it be hard to hook em up?<P><BR>thanx, <BR>coRy||||reg||1
Z||000006||revin||12-17-2001||08:26 AM||||Digital dash? ...huh ok.<BR>A idea for you is to get a third brake light from a car with the light already in the spoiler and take the light out.mount it on the outside of the back window where the org. one would go. I took one off a eclipes and cut it in half (long ways) it fits just under the lip of the roof.You really cannot tell there is one there untill the brakes are on. I get many complements on it! Just a thought.<P>------------------<BR>Revin||||reg||1
