Z||000009||NEPTUNE||12-17-2001||11:26 AM||||You can buy a 13" LED which mounts with 2 screws from J C Whitney for $13 (USD).  I mounted it under the wing in the slot that runs across. You also could mount it abve the rear window. If your'e adding it to a car that already has a 3rd brake light (86 up) connect it to the blue wire  near the drivers side rear speaker.  <BR>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by revin:<BR><B>Digital dash? ...huh ok.<BR>A idea for you is to get a third brake light from a car with the light already in the spoiler and take the light out.mount it on the outside of the back window where the org. one would go. I took one off a eclipes and cut it in half (long ways) it fits just under the lip of the roof.You really cannot tell there is one there untill the brakes are on. I get many complements on it! Just a thought.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
